window.__REDOCS_SEARCH=[{"t":"Book model","u":"data/book-model.html","k":"data","h":["Book model","Five schemas","Entity lifecycle","Reference syntax in pages"],"x":"Book model The Book repository is the single source of truth. An agent in a later session only needs these files to understand the book and continue consistently. Schemas live in the skill's schemas/ and are checked by the Loader + schemas with ajv (JSON Schema 2020-12). <book>/ ├── AGENTS.md rules for agents working on this book ├── book.json title, language, milestones, chapters, plugin settings ├── entities/*.json one array of entities per file ├── pages/<chapter>/<page>/page.json + index.md | index.html | <milestone>.md|html ├── artifacts/<id>/ spec.*, rendered output, receipt.json └── assets/ screenshots/, wireframes/… Five schemas Schema Checks Key points book.schema.json book.json schemaVersion: 1 ; milestone status ∈ superseded/current/planned/target page.schema.json page.json id equals the folder path; variants maps milestone → file; standalone for self-contained HTML entity-file.schema.json entities/*.json ids look like <prefix>:<slug> ; since , until , replaced_by , depends_on artifact-receipt.schema.json receipt.json inputHash is the sha256: of the spec at render time plugin.schema.json plugin.json adapter is a module exporting render() Unknown fields are rejected, except x-* keys, so a typo never slips through silently. Entity lifecycle An entity is alive at milestone m when since ≤ m < until , in the milestone order of book.json ( isAlive in lib/milestone-order-and-lifecycle.mjs ). No since means \"from the first milestone\"; no until means \"never removed\"; replaced_by requires until (RD010). Reference syntax in pages Syntax Markdown HTML fragment Page link [x](page:chapter/page#anchor) href=\"page:…\" Entity [[svc:billing]] , [[svc:billing|label]] as in Markdown, inside text Asset ![x](asset:screenshots/a.png) src=\"asset:…\" Artifact a redocs-embed fence holding JSON <redocs-embed artifact=\"…\"> The output is described in dist/ layout ."},{"t":"dist/ layout","u":"data/dist-layout.html","k":"data","h":["dist/ layout","Generated pages","Determinism"],"x":"dist/ layout Build deletes and rewrites the whole dist/ on every build. Every href / src is relative, so the folder can be moved, zipped or opened from anywhere. Path conventions live in one place: SITE in lib/site-paths-and-urls.mjs . dist/ ├── index.html meta refresh to <current>/index.html ├── finalize-receipt.json written by finalize ├── _redocs/redocs.css, redocs.js shared theme ├── assets/… copied from the book's assets/ ├── artifacts/<id>/<output> copied artifacts with the resize script injected └── <milestone>/ ├── index.html home page for the milestone ├── search-index.js window.__REDOCS_SEARCH = […] ├── <page-id>.html ├── _standalone/<page-id>.html self-contained HTML pages (shown in an iframe) ├── catalog/index.html, catalog/<type>.html ├── changes/<a>-to-<b>.html └── compare/<page-id>/<a>-vs-<b>.html Generated pages Page Built from When Home book.json every milestone Catalog entities/ every milestone; alive entities first, the rest under \"Not at this milestone\" Changes A → B entity lifecycles + page variants each adjacent pair, plus current → last when not adjacent Compare A ↔ B two variants of a page pages whose variants differ for that pair Compare pages iframe the real pages with ?embed=1 (hiding the chrome), so relative links inside stay correct. Determinism No timestamps in the output; displayed dates come from page.json updated . distHash hashes the relative path and content of every file in sorted order, and a test asserts that two builds give the same hash."},{"t":"ADR-002: One page tree per milestone","u":"decisions/milestone-trees.html","k":"decision","h":["ADR-002: One page tree per milestone","Context","Decision","Consequences"],"x":"ADR-002: One page tree per milestone Status : accepted (2026-10-18). Context Readers need to see the book at each milestone (v1, v2, target) and switch between them. Two options: One page tree; JavaScript swaps content for the selected milestone (kept in localStorage ). Build each milestone into a complete tree dist/<milestone>/… . Decision Option 2. Pages without variants are rendered again in every tree; pages with variants render the body of that milestone. Consequences (+) The URL states the milestone; no JavaScript is needed to read the right content; every link is a real file check can verify. (+) The milestone switcher is just a relative link to the same page in another tree. (−) File count grows with pages × milestones. The Kiro Crew dogfood book: 16 pages × 2 milestones → 50 HTML pages, a 59-file zip. (−) One search index per milestone. Details: Milestone and variant resolution ."},{"t":"ADR-001: Own builder instead of Starlight","u":"decisions/own-builder.html","k":"decision","h":["ADR-001: Own builder instead of Starlight","Context","Decision","Consequences"],"x":"ADR-001: Own builder instead of Starlight Status : accepted (2026-10-18). Context Output must open directly over file:// and travel as a zip ( Runtime environment ). Popular static site generators (Astro Starlight, Docusaurus, MkDocs Material) already solve navigation, search and theming, but their search loads its index with fetch() , and some assets use absolute paths. The 2026-10-18 spike confirmed that Chrome blocks fetch() of local files under file:// (CORS, origin null ). The owner also asked for an AI-native tool, not \"a plain Starlight site\": a machine-readable model, a gate, and a plugin contract. Decision Write a small Node builder: multi-page HTML, relative links, runtime data through <script src> , minimal dependencies ( markdown-it , ajv , yazl ). Consequences (+) Full control over the gate: renderers collect diagnostics instead of throwing, so check and build share one render. (+) No large toolchain; the skill is self-contained. (−) Navigation, search and theme are ours to maintain; no plugin ecosystem. (−) Search is simple substring scoring: enough for a few hundred pages, no advanced ranking. Revisit when several people must write at once or the book needs authenticated hosting. Switching renderers (for example to Starlight) stays cheap because the sources are Markdown plus schema-checked JSON."},{"t":"Embedding artifacts","u":"flows/embed-artifact.html","k":"flow","h":["Embedding artifacts","Steps of redocs embed <book> <plugin> <id> --spec <file>","Freshness","Built-in plugins","Display"],"x":"Embedding artifacts Diagrams, wireframes and other generated visuals are artifacts : a spec to edit, an output a plugin renders, and a receipt proving the output matches the spec. The flow lives in lib/command-embed-artifact.mjs ( Embed + plugin registry ). Steps of redocs embed <book> <plugin> <id> --spec <file> Validate the id (a slug) and find the plugin through lib/load-plugin-registry.mjs : built-in plugins under plugins/ , or plugins the book declares in book.json (these need --allow-book-plugins because they run code from the book repository). Check that the spec extension matches the plugin's specExtension ; copy it to artifacts/<id>/spec.<ext> (only one spec.* is kept). Compute inputHash = sha256(spec) . Call adapter.render({specFile, outputFile, options, book, plugin}) in a scratch folder. On success move the output into artifacts/<id>/ . On failure keep the previous output . Write receipt.json . Plugin notices (such as \"a newer archify is available\") go back to the caller but are not stored, so the receipt stays stable across renders. Freshness Check gate reports RD007 when a receipt failed, the output is missing, or the current spec hash differs from inputHash . redocs embed <book> --refresh-stale re-renders every such artifact with the plugin and options recorded in its receipt. Built-in plugins Plugin Spec Notes archify plugin .json Runs archify finalize --quality showcase --json ; a failure reports archify's first diagnostic. See archify . html plugin .html Must be a complete HTML document with no remote resources and no fetch() /XHR. Display On a page, an HTML artifact is an iframe with an \"Open full screen\" link; an image artifact is an <img> . The copy in dist/ gets a postMessage height script so the frame shrinks to its content, capped by the embed's height ."},{"t":"The finalize gate","u":"flows/finalize.html","k":"flow","h":["The finalize gate","Steps","Why the browser gate matches a real reader","Cleanup"],"x":"The finalize gate Finalize is the only evidence an agent may use to say \"the book is done\". SKILL.md says so explicitly: done means finalize exited 0. redocs finalize: check, build, then the browser gate Open full screen Steps Check : the Loader + schemas reads the book; the Renderer renders every page at every milestone in memory; Check gate runs RD000–RD012. Any error stops here, before build ( --strict also fails on warnings). Build : Build reuses the same render that was checked, writes dist/ and computes distHash . Browser gate : Chrome CDP checker opens every HTML page (artifacts and assets excluded) over file:// in headless Chrome with a throwaway profile, collecting console errors, exceptions, failed requests and pages that do not load. Receipt : dist/finalize-receipt.json records checks, build and browser results. Why the browser gate matches a real reader Chrome runs without file-relaxing flags such as --allow-file-access-from-files . The spike showed that a blocked fetch() under file:// is exactly the kind of failure the gate must catch, and the checker caught it. REDOCS_CHROME_NO_SANDBOX=1 only turns off Chrome's process sandbox (needed inside an already-sandboxed agent shell); it does not change what a page may load. Cleanup Chrome is closed with Browser.close , then SIGTERM / SIGKILL if needed; the temporary profile ( redocs-cdp-* ) is removed in finally ."},{"t":"Milestone and variant resolution","u":"flows/milestones.html","k":"flow","h":["Milestone and variant resolution","Picking a page body at milestone m (resolveVariant)","Checking entities per milestone","Comparison pairs (comparisonPairs)","Promote"],"x":"Milestone and variant resolution All rules live in lib/milestone-order-and-lifecycle.mjs , shared by the Renderer and Build . Picking a page body at milestone m ( resolveVariant ) Page Shows at m No variants the shared entry file (default index.md , then index.html ) Has a variant for m that file None for m, one for an earlier milestone the nearest earlier variant, with an \"inherited from …\" notice None for m or any earlier milestone a \"does not exist at this milestone yet\" page Checking entities per milestone Milestone-specific variants are checked strictly: every [[entity]] must be alive at that milestone, otherwise RD005. Shared pages (vision, proposals) may mention future or removed entities; their chips show a \"from v2\" or \"removed in …\" badge instead of failing. Example: CLI and commands has a v2 variant that mentions Presentation mode (since v2); the v1 variant may not. Comparison pairs ( comparisonPairs ) Every adjacent pair of milestones, plus current → last milestone when they are not adjacent. This book (v1, v2) has a single pair, v1 → v2. Promote redocs promote <book> v2 marks earlier milestones superseded , makes v2 current , and prints the pages and entities the owner should confirm. It never rewrites content: what really changed is the owner's call. Milestones only move forward."},{"t":"archify","u":"integrations/archify.html","k":"integration","h":["archify","Adapter contract (plugins/archify/adapter-archify-finalize.mjs)","Lessons from real use"],"x":"archify archify skill is a skill that renders diagrams from schema-checked JSON (architecture, workflow, sequence, dataflow, lifecycle) into self-contained HTML with inline SVG. ReDocs does not fork it; archify plugin calls archify's own finalize gate (validate, deliver, strict check, browser check). Adapter contract ( plugins/archify/adapter-archify-finalize.mjs ) Step Details Find archify $REDOCS_ARCHIFY → book.json plugins.archify.path → ~/.kiro/crew/skills/archify → ~/.claude/skills/archify Check --type architecture , workflow , sequence , dataflow , lifecycle Run node bin/archify.mjs finalize <type> candidate.json diagram.html --quality showcase --json in a scratch folder, 300 s timeout Environment Maps REDOCS_CHROME_NO_SANDBOX to ARCHIFY_CHROME_NO_SANDBOX and REDOCS_CHROME to ARCHIFY_CHROME Result Keeps status , gates and up to 10 diagnostics; update notices are only relayed to the caller Running in scratch keeps archify's sidecar files ( *.finalize.json , *.browser-check.json …) out of the book repository. Lessons from real use archify's viewer ships en and zh-CN only; non-English books keep English diagram labels and explain them in page prose. Sequence diagrams: keep messages at least 30px apart, keep participant labels short, omit meta.viewBox . The first sequence diagram of the Kiro Crew book needed four repair rounds; both diagrams of this book passed on the first render thanks to those tips. TODO(owner): Upgrade archify from 3.0.1 to 3.1.0? ReDocs never updates it on its own."},{"t":"Headless Chrome","u":"integrations/chrome.html","k":"integration","h":["Headless Chrome","Finding a browser","Per page","Sandbox"],"x":"Headless Chrome The Chrome CDP checker ( lib/chrome-cdp-file-protocol-check.mjs ) drives Chrome / Chromium through the Chrome DevTools Protocol over --remote-debugging-pipe : fd 3 takes commands, fd 4 returns events, each JSON message ends with a NUL byte. No port and no WebSocket are needed; the approach comes from archify. Finding a browser $REDOCS_CHROME , then /Applications/Google Chrome.app/… and /Applications/Chromium.app/… on macOS, then google-chrome , chromium … on PATH . If none is found the result is ERR_REDOCS_NO_CHROME with a hint. Per page Target.createTarget + attachToTarget (flattened sessions). Enable Page , Runtime , Log , Network ; set a 1280×900 viewport (optionally dark mode). Page.navigate to file://… , wait for loadEventFired (15 s timeout), then let the page settle. Collect Runtime.exceptionThrown , console.error , error-level Log.entryAdded , and Network.loadingFailed . Optionally evaluate a JS expression or capture a screenshot ( scripts/screenshot-pages.mjs uses this for visual review). Sandbox Inside a Kiro Crew agent shell Chrome cannot initialize its own sandbox ( sandbox initialization failed: Operation not permitted ), hence REDOCS_CHROME_NO_SANDBOX=1 . Running as root adds --no-sandbox automatically."},{"t":"Runtime environment","u":"network/topology.html","k":"infra","h":["Runtime environment (v2)","Behaviour to keep"],"x":"Runtime environment (v2) The v2 variant is a proposal . See Proposal: phase 2 . file:// stays the primary environment, as in v1. The phase 2 backlog lists \"optional internal hosting\" as a direction. TODO(owner): Does phase 2 need internal hosting (for example private S3 + CloudFront), or stay pure file://? If hosting, state the authentication requirement. Behaviour to keep Every row of the v1 table must still hold; if hosting is added, the output must work both ways and the browser gate must check both."},{"t":"System context","u":"overview/system-context.html","k":"overview","h":["System context","Technology","Quality attributes"],"x":"System context The Owner (author) gives instructions; the AI agent reads SKILL.md + references and calls the redocs CLI . The CLI runs the engine ( Loader + schemas , Renderer , Check gate , Build ) over the Book repository and writes dist/ . The Reader opens dist/index.html straight from disk. Diagrams come from archify plugin calling the archify skill skill; Chrome / Chromium is the final gate. ReDocs v1: from the owner's instructions to static HTML a reader opens over file:// Open full screen What to notice in the diagram: The main path has no server : everything is a Node process run on demand plus files on disk. The book repository is separate from the skill : the skill can be upgraded without touching books; each system has its own book. Chrome sits at the end , opening exactly the files a reader will open, under the same file:// rules. Technology Area Choice Runtime Node ≥ 18, ES modules Dependencies (pinned exactly) markdown-it , ajv , yazl Tests node:test , including a real archify render and the browser gate Browser gate Headless Chrome/Chromium over --remote-debugging-pipe Quality attributes Deterministic : the same sources give the same distHash ; the zip has fixed order and mtimes. Offline : no fetch() , no remote resources (RD009); runtime data loads through <script src> . No lost artifacts : a failed render keeps the previous output and the receipt records the error. Agent-readable errors : every problem is a diagnostic with a code, file, JSON pointer or line, and a fix hint."},{"t":"Proposal: phase 2","u":"proposals/phase-2.html","k":"proposal","h":["Proposal: phase 2","Context","Proposed decisions","Impact","Alternatives considered","Rollout"],"x":"Proposal: phase 2 Status : draft. Milestone : v2. Context Version 0.1.0 (v1) covers phase 1 and was dogfooded on a book about Kiro Crew. The implementation plan lists the phase 2 backlog: presentation/slide mode, PDF export of one chapter, optional internal hosting. The dogfood added two items: interface strings stay English inside non-English books, and entity file names mix singular and plural. Proposed decisions Item New component Source Interface strings follow the book language (en, vi) Localized UI strings dogfood finding Present one chapter as slides Presentation mode plan backlog Export one chapter to PDF Chapter PDF export , using Chrome CDP checker plan backlog Always plural entity file names change to Authoring commands dogfood finding Optional internal hosting not decided plan backlog TODO(owner): Priority and timing for each item? Impact New entities since: v2 : Localized UI strings , Presentation mode , Chapter PDF export . Pages with a v2 variant: CLI and commands , Runtime environment . The generated Changes v1 → v2 page summarises the above. Alternatives considered Slides with an external library (reveal.js): capable, but a large dependency that must be bundled offline. Preferred: turn each ## into a slide with the theme's own CSS/JS. PDF with a dedicated library : not needed; headless Chrome is already there for the gate ( Page.printToPDF ). Rollout mod:ui-i18n : a string table in the theme and shell, picked by book.json language , defaulting to en . add-entity always writes plural file names and still reads old singular files. present : writes dist/<m>/present/<chapter>.html . export-pdf : prints the chapter page through CDP Page.printToPDF . Every step ships with tests and a green finalize on the dogfood books. TODO(owner): Review this proposal (draft → review → accepted)."},{"t":"Check codes","u":"reference/check-codes.html","k":"reference","h":["Check codes","Design of the codes"],"x":"Check codes Check gate reports diagnostics as SEVERITY CODE file pointer|line: message (or JSON with --json ), plus a hint . The full table with fixes lives in the skill's references/check-codes.md ; a test keeps it in sync with RULE_CODES in the code. Code Severity Meaning RD000 error JSON cannot be read or parsed RD001 error Schema violation; page id differs from its folder; duplicate entity id RD002 error/warning A chapter lists an unknown or duplicate page; a page is in no chapter RD003 error Broken page: link or #anchor RD004 error Entity not registered RD005 error A variant mentions an entity that does not exist at its milestone RD006 error/warning Bad variant milestone or missing source; a stray source the page never renders RD007 error/warning Artifact missing, failed or older than its spec; artifact embedded nowhere RD008 error Asset does not exist RD009 error Remote resource (not offline) RD010 error Entity graph: dependencies, replacement, since/until RD011 warning Open TODO(owner) question RD012 error Not exactly one current milestone; duplicate milestone/chapter ids Design of the codes Codes are stable so agents and people can look them up across versions. A problem seen at several milestones is reported once: a broken link on a shared page does not name a milestone. RD011 is a warning on purpose: a book with open questions still builds, but the owner sees what is left. --strict turns it into a failure. The \"stray source\" warning (RD006) came from the Kiro Crew dogfood: an index.md silently shadowed an index.html and a wireframe disappeared without any error."},{"t":"CLI and commands","u":"services/cli.html","k":"module","h":["CLI and commands","Commands","Environment variables"],"x":"CLI and commands The redocs CLI runs as node <skill-dir>/bin/redocs.mjs <command> . Every command prints a human summary, or a JSON receipt with --json . Exit codes: 0 success, 1 content or check failure, 2 usage error. The v2 variant is a proposal , not implemented. See Proposal: phase 2 . Commands All v1 commands stay; added: Command (proposed) Does Component present <book> <chapter> [--milestone] Present one chapter as slides, one slide per ## Presentation mode export-pdf <book> <chapter> [--milestone] Print one chapter to PDF with headless Chrome Chapter PDF export Every page build writes shows its interface strings in the book's language ( Localized UI strings ). TODO(owner): Confirm the command names, and whether present writes HTML into dist/ or opens directly. Environment variables As in v1."},{"t":"Components","u":"services/overview.html","k":"service","h":["Components","Key boundaries"],"x":"Components ReDocs is one skill package ( skill/redocs/ ) holding the agent contract, the CLI, the engine and the plugins. The Catalog lists every component; this page shows the boundaries. Layer Components Main files Agent contract SKILL.md + references SKILL.md , references/*.md , templates/book-starter/AGENTS.md Command interface redocs CLI bin/redocs.mjs Authoring Authoring commands , Promote lib/command-init-book.mjs , lib/command-add-page-entity-variant.mjs , lib/command-promote-milestone.mjs Model Loader + schemas lib/load-book-from-directory.mjs , lib/validate-book-schemas.mjs , schemas/*.schema.json Rendering Renderer lib/render-book-pages.mjs , lib/render-markdown-with-redocs-extensions.mjs , lib/render-html-fragment-with-redocs-extensions.mjs , lib/render-redocs-references.mjs Checking Check gate lib/check-book-rules.mjs , lib/command-check-book.mjs Publishing Build , Pack lib/command-build-book-site.mjs , lib/build-generated-pages.mjs , lib/render-page-shell-layout.mjs , lib/command-pack-book-zip.mjs Final gate Finalize , Chrome CDP checker lib/command-finalize-book.mjs , lib/chrome-cdp-file-protocol-check.mjs Plugins Embed + plugin registry , archify plugin , html plugin lib/command-embed-artifact.mjs , lib/load-plugin-registry.mjs , plugins/*/ Reader UI (theme) assets/theme/redocs.css , assets/theme/redocs.js Key boundaries The loader never throws for content : broken JSON, schema errors and duplicate ids all become diagnostics. Only a missing book.json stops it. Renderers record, they do not judge : links, entities, embeds and assets are recorded in the render context; Check gate decides what is an error once every page at every milestone is rendered (anchors need that). Build does not check itself : it renders and writes; finalize combines check, build and the browser. Commands and flags: CLI and commands ."},{"t":"Reader experience","u":"ux/reader.html","k":"wireframe","h":["Reader experience","A page with a diagram","A generated Changes page","Accessibility"],"x":"Reader experience The Reader opens index.html and lands on the current milestone. The screenshots below were taken from this book with scripts/screenshot-pages.mjs (1280×900). A page with a diagram Header : book title, milestone bar (planned milestones have a dashed border), search box ( / focuses it), theme toggle. Sidebar : chapters in book.json order, then Catalog and Changes. Right column : an \"On this page\" table of contents when a page has at least two h2/h3 headings. A generated Changes page Accessibility Skip link, nav / main landmarks, visible focus, horizontally scrolling tables on narrow screens, prefers-reduced-motion respected; below 760px the sidebar becomes a toggle menu. TODO(owner): Should finalize add an automated contrast check (axe)?"},{"t":"Why ReDocs exists","u":"vision/why.html","k":"vision","h":["Why ReDocs exists","The problem","Founding decisions (owner session, 2026-10-18)","What \"AI native\" means here","Non-goals (phase 1)"],"x":"Why ReDocs exists ReDocs is a skill that lets an AI agent write and maintain a system design book on the instructions of the system's owner. The book covers the system's whole life: the original idea, the current state, proposed changes to present or hand to developers, and the long-term target. The problem Documentation for a large system (many microservices, data flows, integrations, networks, infrastructure) usually falls into one of two traps: Written by hand : expensive, so it goes stale; every author writes differently. Written freely by AI : fast, but it invents things, drifts between sessions, and nobody can tell whether the book is still consistent. ReDocs makes the AI the main author but constrains it with a machine-readable model and a deterministic gate . Founding decisions (owner session, 2026-10-18) Question Decision Who writes, who reads? The AI writes on a person's instructions; the book is mainly for people. Where do docs live? One book repository per system, never inside a code repository. Automatic updates? No. The book changes when the author asks, and it may describe a system before it exists. Formats? Markdown for simple parts, HTML where layout matters, embedded artifacts from AI tools such as archify. How is it read? Opened straight from disk over file:// ; shareable as a zip. Versions? Global milestones (v1, v2, target) are system states; Git keeps edit history. What \"AI native\" means here The agent is the authoring interface; people do not hand-edit HTML. A machine-readable source of truth: the book model . A deterministic gate: work is done only when finalize passes. One plugin contract for content tools, archify first ( Embedding artifacts ). Non-goals (phase 1) Multi-author collaboration, a server, authentication, syncing from code, a chatbot inside the book, generating diagrams from entities, WYSIWYG editing. Next: System context ."},{"t":"AI agent","u":"catalog/actor.html#app-agent","k":"actor","h":["app:agent"],"x":"Reads SKILL.md and calls the redocs CLI"},{"t":"Owner (author)","u":"catalog/actor.html#app-owner","k":"actor","h":["app:owner"],"x":"Owns the documented system; gives instructions and answers TODO(owner) questions"},{"t":"Reader","u":"catalog/actor.html#app-reader","k":"actor","h":["app:reader"],"x":"Stakeholder or developer opening dist/index.html over file://"},{"t":"Book repository","u":"catalog/datastore.html#db-book-repo","k":"datastore","h":["db:book-repo"],"x":"book.json, pages/, entities/, artifacts/, assets/, AGENTS.md: the source of truth"},{"t":"dist/","u":"catalog/datastore.html#db-dist","k":"datastore","h":["db:dist"],"x":"Static HTML site, one tree per milestone; git-ignored"},{"t":"archify skill","u":"catalog/external.html#ext-archify","k":"external","h":["ext:archify"],"x":"Renders architecture, workflow, sequence, dataflow and lifecycle diagrams"},{"t":"Chrome / Chromium","u":"catalog/external.html#ext-chrome","k":"external","h":["ext:chrome"],"x":"Headless browser for the browser check (REDOCS_CHROME)"},{"t":"Authoring commands","u":"catalog/module.html#mod-authoring","k":"module","h":["mod:authoring"],"x":"init, add-page, add-entity, add-variant"},{"t":"Build","u":"catalog/module.html#mod-build","k":"module","h":["mod:build"],"x":"Page shell, generated pages, search index, artifact and asset copies, distHash"},{"t":"Chrome CDP checker","u":"catalog/module.html#mod-cdp","k":"module","h":["mod:cdp"],"x":"Headless Chrome over --remote-debugging-pipe: console errors, failed requests, screenshots"},{"t":"Check gate","u":"catalog/module.html#mod-check","k":"module","h":["mod:check"],"x":"Rules RD000-RD012 over the rendered model"},{"t":"redocs CLI","u":"catalog/module.html#mod-cli","k":"module","h":["mod:cli"],"x":"bin/redocs.mjs: parses arguments, runs commands, prints text or JSON receipts, exit codes 0/1/2"},{"t":"Embed + plugin registry","u":"catalog/module.html#mod-embed","k":"module","h":["mod:embed"],"x":"Copies the spec, runs the adapter, writes a receipt with the spec sha256; --refresh-stale"},{"t":"Finalize","u":"catalog/module.html#mod-finalize","k":"module","h":["mod:finalize"],"x":"check, build, then the file:// browser check; writes finalize-receipt.json"},{"t":"Loader + schemas","u":"catalog/module.html#mod-loader","k":"module","h":["mod:loader"],"x":"Reads a book and validates it with ajv (JSON Schema 2020-12); problems become diagnostics"},{"t":"Pack","u":"catalog/module.html#mod-pack","k":"module","h":["mod:pack"],"x":"Deterministic zip of dist/ (yazl)"},{"t":"Chapter PDF export","u":"catalog/module.html#mod-pdf-export","k":"module","h":["mod:pdf-export"],"x":"Proposed: print one chapter to PDF"},{"t":"Presentation mode","u":"catalog/module.html#mod-presentation","k":"module","h":["mod:presentation"],"x":"Proposed: present one chapter as slides"},{"t":"Promote","u":"catalog/module.html#mod-promote","k":"module","h":["mod:promote"],"x":"Moves the current milestone pointer and lists what to review"},{"t":"Renderer","u":"catalog/module.html#mod-renderer","k":"module","h":["mod:renderer"],"x":"Markdown (markdown-it) and HTML fragments with page:, asset:, [[entity]] and redocs-embed; renders every page at every milestone in memory"},{"t":"SKILL.md + references","u":"catalog/module.html#mod-skill-md","k":"module","h":["mod:skill-md"],"x":"Agent contract and intent router; six reference documents"},{"t":"Localized UI strings","u":"catalog/module.html#mod-ui-i18n","k":"module","h":["mod:ui-i18n"],"x":"Proposed: UI string table selected by book.json language"},{"t":"archify plugin","u":"catalog/plugin.html#plugin-archify","k":"plugin","h":["plugin:archify"],"x":"Runs archify finalize in a scratch folder and copies the HTML"},{"t":"html plugin","u":"catalog/plugin.html#plugin-html","k":"plugin","h":["plugin:html"],"x":"Wireframes, mockups and other tools output; rejects remote resources and fetch()"}];
